## Plan (raid 94edd2)

Premise checked: nothing merged since this ticket's creation touches gaze_setup.py,
gaze_close.py or skills/gaze/.

Design reading: seat reports print from `scripts/wait-roster.py` on exit 0 ("the call
that waits for the roster"), not from `gaze_close.py`, which runs after the reports are
read (it consumes the attribution and comment files written from them). Nothing printed
on exit 1 or 3. Both outputs bounded by a fixed cap with a truncation line; no flags.

Actions: (1) Step 0: `python3 scripts/gaze_wall_analysis.py 2026-10-27T10:45Z` (it takes
the cut as argv[1], no `--help`); preliminary: setup median 39 s, closing 37 s, n=185,
about 1.7 git-read calls per run before launch; classify 10 setup and 10 closing
sequences by hand, record go/no-go in the log. (2) Test, then `bounded_diff` in
gaze_setup.py, printed after the roster against its anchor. (3) Test, then wait-roster.py
prints `== <name>.md ==` and each report, bounded in total, excluding `.part` and stale
files. (4) One-line updates: skills/gaze/SKILL.md § 1, references/setup-and-breaker.md,
references/panel.md § Collection.

First tests: tests/test_gaze_setup.py, temp repo via `make_repo`, asserts the diff stat
and the changed hunk against the PR base, and a truncation case bounded under the cap;
tests/test_wait_roster.py, three reports plus a `.part` and a stale one, all three bodies
printed, the others not, nothing on exit 1.
